# QA replay of clearing the stash desk (owner, 2026-10-26: "We need an option to clear the desk because it quickly gets
# messy"; from the coordinator's options, "Button + fresh after raid"; docs/DESIGN.md §4, *The stash desk*, *Clearing the
# page*): CLEAR at the head line's right empties the page at once, every region the dashed frame of a region never read,
# its pins and the card pointed at gone, and the notice "Desk cleared." offers UNDO, which puts the page back as it was,
# its pins with it; UNDO goes with the notice; the next reading is the mode's first again. A developer build plays it with
# --dev-view --dev-script; how to run it and what each still must show: desk-clear.md beside this file. Times are in
# seconds.

# The tour that opens by itself in a --dev-view session ends first, and its notice is waited out.
tour end
map customs
wait 7

# The first reading; its cells come in and its totals count up, then the page stands, CLEAR at the head line's right.
# The LEDX pinned, the Zhuk's cell pointed at: its card in the rail, the pin's line at the rail's foot.
desk 1
wait 7
desk pin stash 8 0
desk point backpack 0 0
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk-clear\before

# CLEAR: the page empty at once, every region as never read, the head line KEEP 0 · 0 · 0 alone, CLEAR gone; the rail's
# card and pin gone, the rail's hint in their place; "Desk cleared." with UNDO at the top.
desk clear
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk-clear\cleared

# UNDO: the page as it was, standing at once (nothing comes in, the totals don't count up), the LEDX's pin back; the
# notice gone.
desk undo
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk-clear\undone

# CLEAR again, and the notice waited out (8 s): UNDO goes with it ("desk undo" then says no notice offers it).
desk clear
wait 9
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk-clear\expired
desk undo

# A reading after CLEAR is the mode's first again: it comes in whole.
desk 1
wait 7
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk-clear\read-again
exit
